List containers|docker ps -a|Lists running and stopped containers.|Find exited workloads and current image/port assignments.|STATUS shows running, exited or restarting; PORTS shows published mappings.|CONTAINER ID IMAGE COMMAND CREATED STATUS PORTS NAMES|Read-only; requires access to the intended daemon, which is privileged.
Inspect configuration|docker inspect CONTAINER|Returns detailed runtime configuration and state as JSON.|Compare effective command, mounts, network and exit state with expectations.|State.ExitCode and State.Error describe termination; Mounts and NetworkSettings expose runtime wiring.|[{"State":{"Status":"exited","ExitCode":1}}]|Read-only but output can reveal environment secrets; replace CONTAINER.
Bounded logs|docker logs --since 10m --tail 100 CONTAINER|Reads a bounded recent set of captured container logs.|Find startup and runtime errors near the incident.|--since restricts time and --tail limits lines; use timestamps when correlation is needed.|application startup failed: ...|Read-only; log driver support varies and output may contain secrets.
Resource snapshot|docker stats --no-stream|Prints one resource-usage snapshot for running containers.|Spot memory pressure, CPU usage and I/O differences.|Compare MEM USAGE / LIMIT with configured constraints; a single sample can miss peaks.|NAME CPU % MEM USAGE / LIMIT NET I/O BLOCK I/O|Read-only; combine with historical metrics for capacity conclusions.
Published ports|docker port CONTAINER|Lists container-port to host-address mappings.|Confirm whether and where a service is published.|127.0.0.1 binds locally; 0.0.0.0 exposes all IPv4 host interfaces subject to other controls.|8080/tcp -> 127.0.0.1:8080|Read-only; publishing does not prove the application is listening.
Network inspection|docker network inspect NETWORK|Displays a network's driver, addressing and connected endpoints.|Check whether communicating containers share the intended network.|Containers lists endpoint attachments; IPAM describes configured address pools.|"Driver": "bridge", "Containers": {...}|Read-only; inspect the intended daemon and network.
Volume inspection|docker volume inspect VOLUME|Displays volume metadata and driver configuration.|Identify durable storage before replacing a container.|Mountpoint is daemon-host storage location for relevant drivers; Options may describe external storage.|"Name": "app-data", "Driver": "local"|Read-only; never infer a volume is disposable from lack of a running container.
Storage accounting|docker system df|Summarizes storage used by images, containers, volumes and cache.|Locate the type of space growth before cleanup.|RECLAIMABLE estimates unused storage, not whether the data is valuable.|TYPE TOTAL ACTIVE SIZE RECLAIMABLE|Read-only; do not automatically follow with prune, especially for volumes.
Image metadata|docker image inspect IMAGE|Shows image configuration, identifiers and platform metadata.|Verify the deployed image identity and startup defaults.|RepoDigests identifies content references when available; Config contains entrypoint, command and user.|"RepoDigests": ["repo@sha256:..."]|Read-only; metadata may contain build-time configuration.
Render Compose model|docker compose config|Renders and validates the effective Compose configuration.|Find variable substitution, merged-file and service-wiring mistakes.|Read the resolved service settings rather than only source fragments.|services: ...|Can expose interpolated secrets; requires the Compose plugin and the intended project files.
Compose service state|docker compose ps -a|Lists containers belonging to the current Compose project.|Check missing, exited or unhealthy services together.|State and Health are separate; absence may indicate the wrong project or uncreated service.|NAME IMAGE SERVICE CREATED STATUS PORTS|Read-only; project selection depends on directory and options.
Daemon information|docker info|Reports daemon configuration, storage driver and runtime environment.|Check rootless mode, platform and daemon-level differences.|Compare Security Options, Docker Root Dir and driver fields with the expected host.|Storage Driver: overlay2|Read-only; output contains host details and access to the daemon is privileged.
Client and server versions|docker version|Reports Docker client and daemon versions and API compatibility.|Identify whether a command mismatch comes from the client or selected daemon.|Client and Server are distinct sections; a missing server section can indicate connection failure.|Client: Version ... Server: Engine Version ...|Read-only; confirm the intended context before diagnosing a remote daemon.
Context selection evidence|docker context ls|Lists configured Docker endpoints and the active context.|Avoid inspecting or changing the wrong host.|The asterisk marks the current context; Docker Endpoint identifies the daemon connection.|NAME DESCRIPTION DOCKER ENDPOINT|Read-only; endpoint names alone do not prove environment ownership.
Image inventory|docker image ls --digests|Lists local image references and recorded digests.|Compare cached artifacts with the intended release identity.|REPOSITORY and TAG are names; DIGEST is content identity when available and can be absent for local builds.|REPOSITORY TAG DIGEST IMAGE ID CREATED SIZE|Read-only; several tags can refer to one image.
Image layer history|docker image history --no-trunc IMAGE|Displays the image's layer history and build-command metadata.|Investigate image growth or accidentally embedded build data.|CREATED BY describes recorded build instructions; SIZE is layer contribution, not necessarily unique disk usage.|IMAGE CREATED CREATED BY SIZE COMMENT|Read-only but may reveal secrets embedded in old build arguments or instructions; protect output.
Build a tagged image|docker build --tag app:review .|Builds an image from the selected context and Dockerfile.|Produce a repeatable candidate artifact from reviewed inputs.|Step output shows build stages and cache use; the final tag identifies the local result, not registry publication.|Successfully tagged app:review|Executes Dockerfile instructions and can use network/build resources. Review context exclusions and base images first.
Build with a secret mount|docker build --secret id=registry_token,src=TOKEN_FILE --tag app:review .|Makes a file available to BuildKit secret mounts during a build.|Allow authenticated build steps without copying the credential into image layers.|The Dockerfile must consume the matching secret ID; a successful build does not prove application code avoided logging it.|Build completed; image tagged app:review|Uses a local credential. Review Dockerfile handling, permissions and logs; never substitute ARG for a secret blindly.
Run an isolated local test|docker run --rm --name app-check -p 127.0.0.1:8080:8080 IMAGE|Starts a disposable container with one loopback-bound published port.|Check a candidate service locally before deployment.|The foreground output is application stdout/stderr; --rm removes this container after exit, not every external volume.|Application listening on 8080|Runs image code and binds a local port. Use a trusted image and avoid production credentials/data.
Container process list|docker top CONTAINER|Displays processes running in a container from the daemon's perspective.|Inspect wrappers and child processes without requiring ps inside the image.|PID/PPID identify process relationships; displayed identifiers may correspond to host process IDs.|UID PID PPID C STIME TTY TIME CMD|Read-only; process arguments can reveal sensitive values.
Execute a diagnostic|docker exec CONTAINER id|Runs id in an already-running container.|Check the identity used by an exec process in the container context.|uid, gid and groups describe this process; application processes may deliberately use different identities.|uid=1000(app) gid=1000(app)|The command is read-only, but exec permits arbitrary actions. Confirm container and avoid dumping secret environments.
Graceful container stop|docker stop --time 30 CONTAINER|Requests termination and allows a bounded grace period before forced stopping.|Give a service time to drain and flush during an approved shutdown.|The printed container name confirms completion of the stop operation; inspect exit state and application evidence.|CONTAINER|Stops a workload. Check availability, stop signal, data handling and restart expectations first.
Copy a diagnostic file|docker cp CONTAINER:/var/log/app/diagnostic.txt ./diagnostic.txt|Copies a selected file from a container to the local filesystem.|Preserve a scoped diagnostic artifact before container replacement.|No output normally means the copy succeeded; inspect destination size and content separately.|No output on success|Writes a local file and may expose confidential data. Choose a protected destination and a narrow path.
Filesystem changes|docker diff CONTAINER|Lists paths changed in the container's writable layer.|Investigate runtime modifications not represented in the image.|A means added, C changed and D deleted; mounted-volume contents are outside this writable-layer diff.|C /etc/app.conf|Read-only; this is not a full backup or a content diff.
Daemon event stream|docker events --since 10m --until 0s|Displays recent daemon events over a bounded interval ending now.|Correlate starts, exits and health transitions with an incident.|Each event has a timestamp, object type, action and attributes; retained history may be limited.|container die ... exitCode=1|Read-only event observation; daemon event history is not a durable audit archive.
Network inventory|docker network ls|Lists networks known to the selected Docker daemon.|Check intended bridge/network names before inspecting membership.|DRIVER identifies the network implementation; SCOPE describes its visibility.|NETWORK ID NAME DRIVER SCOPE|Read-only; inspect individual networks to see actual attached containers.
Volume inventory|docker volume ls|Lists named volumes known to the daemon.|Inventory persistent storage before deployment or cleanup.|DRIVER and VOLUME NAME identify storage objects; a listed volume is not proof of a valid backup.|DRIVER VOLUME NAME|Read-only; do not infer disposability from absence of a running container.
Compose bounded logs|docker compose logs --since 10m --tail 100 SERVICE|Reads recent logs for one service in a Compose project.|Investigate a startup failure without dumping every service's history.|Prefixes identify service/container instances; --tail limits each container's retained lines.|api-1  error: connection refused|Read-only; verify Compose project/files and protect secret-bearing output.
Compose deployment|docker compose up -d SERVICE|Creates or reconciles a selected Compose service and its required dependencies.|Apply a reviewed local or single-host application configuration.|Started or Recreated reports lifecycle changes; inspect health and application behavior afterward.|Container project-api-1 Started|Mutates workloads and may recreate containers. Review resolved config, images, volumes and availability first.
Export an image archive|docker image save --output app-image.tar IMAGE|Writes image layers and metadata to a local archive.|Transfer a specific image to an approved offline environment.|The archive is an image artifact, not a container data-volume backup. Verify its digest and destination size separately.|app-image.tar created|Writes potentially large and sensitive image data; ensure adequate disk space and artifact access controls.
